# Cursor Rules — NEXUS-OpenCode-Plugins

## Project Context

This workspace is managed by the Nexus platform.
Treat all project memory and coordination artifacts as architecture-critical.

## Code Style

- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Prefer named exports over default exports
- Use early returns to reduce nesting
- Keep functions under 50 lines where possible

## Architecture

- Follow existing patterns in the codebase
- Document decisions as ADRs when making architectural changes
- Preserve auditability — commit early and often

## Testing

- Write tests for new functionality
- Maintain existing test coverage
- Run the test suite before committing

## Security

- Never expose secrets in code or logs
- Read secrets only from environment variables
- Never commit .env files
